\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The authorization guard as a decision system. The four property predicates evaluate independently in $\{\top ,\bot ,?\}$; their Kleene conjunction is read by the truth-biased guard, which permits $a^+$ only on unanimous $\top $, rejects on any $\bot $ (Theorem\nonbreakingspace \ref  {thm:soundness}), and abstains on an unresolved $?$ with no $\bot $. Removing any predicate deletes one incoming edge to the conjunction and thereby its matched harm block (Theorem\nonbreakingspace \ref  {thm:necessity}).\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:guard}{{2}{5}{The authorization guard as a decision system. The four property predicates evaluate independently in $\{\top ,\bot ,?\}$; their Kleene conjunction is read by the truth-biased guard, which permits $a^+$ only on unanimous $\top $, rejects on any $\bot $ (Theorem~\ref {thm:soundness}), and abstains on an unresolved $?$ with no $\bot $. Removing any predicate deletes one incoming edge to the conjunction and thereby its matched harm block (Theorem~\ref {thm:necessity}).\relax }{figure.caption.13}{}}
